1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,997
(Episode 5)

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:04,500
You think you're pulling the strings,

3
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:09,380
when you're actually the one being played.

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,680
The more clueless you are,

5
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:19,820
the harder you dance to their tune.

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,300
Please, save Kataoka

7
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,377
and Odajima.

8
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,837
I told you, I have no
obligation to step in.

9
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:35,960
But.

10
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:38,120
Kataoka did this for our clan.

11
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:43,740
You made this mess.
Why should I clean it up?

12
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,620
Look at how many of us there are.

13
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,320
What can you do with just one knife?

14
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,220
You don't stand a chance.

15
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:06,520
You're right.

16
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:09,580
However,

17
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:14,420
it's more than enough to kill me.

18
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:17,777
What are you doing?

19
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:19,840
Take us to your boss.

20
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,440
If you don't, he'll slit my throat.

21
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:27,390
If we die, the Kirii Clan will retaliate.

22
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:31,237
And whoever's pulling the
strings will have their plans ruined.

23
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:33,440
Right after I kill you, I'll
follow you to the grave.

24
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:34,929
Good.

25
00:01:35,012 --> 00:01:36,640
That's my wife.

26
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:39,420
Let's see if you've got the guts!

27
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,640
Don't underestimate

28
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:44,740
the resolve of an ex-yakuza!

29
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:57,520
Stop.

30
00:02:33,779 --> 00:02:35,017
Well done.

31
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,157
- Impressive, isn't he?
- Yes.

32
00:02:38,784 --> 00:02:40,786
Don't use karate to pick fights, okay?

33
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:41,869
Okay.

34
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:46,680
You'll get him next time.

35
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:49,603
I could never stand that guy.

36
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:53,380
He beat me at everything.

37
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:56,480
I could never tell what
was going on in his head.

38
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:59,137
And yet,

39
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:01,364
my old man

40
00:03:02,224 --> 00:03:04,100
always favored him over me.

41
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,496
Go kill Kataoka.

42
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:14,820
Is Kataoka still alive?

43
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,532
Make it quick.

44
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:21,120
Oh, right.

45
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:23,980
You're the boss now.

46
00:03:24,996 --> 00:03:27,349
Huh? Are you mocking me?

47
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,980
Huh?

48
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:34,260
What? What's your problem?

49
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:47,160
Those two and us,

50
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:49,380
we go way back.

51
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:53,000
Letting civilians get killed

52
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,060
would be a disgrace to the clan.

53
00:03:58,140 --> 00:03:59,737
Please, save Kataoka

54
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:01,560
and Odajima.

55
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,985
"The Journey To Killing You Season 2"

56
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:33,760
Ihashi-san.

57
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,540
You...

58
00:05:57,380 --> 00:05:58,700
You look familiar.

59
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:03,420
Where have I seen you before?

60
00:06:09,703 --> 00:06:12,055
I hate idiots and I hate wasting time.

61
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:15,600
So I'll make this quick.

62
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:22,740
The only reason you're still breathing

63
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,527
is because keeping you
alive was more profitable.

64
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:27,929
However,

65
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:32,440
since keeping you alive
no longer serves a purpose,

66
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:43,540
I'll just kill you.

67
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:53,054
Time to die.

68
00:07:10,055 --> 00:07:11,348
Kataoka-san.

69
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:13,600
Kataoka-san!

70
00:07:15,352 --> 00:07:17,192
What would you do if
something happened to me?

71
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:21,560
I won't let that happen.

72
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:24,680
This time, I'll protect you no matter what.

73
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:21,320
Looks like you're having fun.

74
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,400
Count me in.

75
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:27,300
Kanto's Largest Syndicate,

76
00:08:27,841 --> 00:08:29,259
Chairman of the Kotoku-kai,

77
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:31,594
Hikari Hanao.

78
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:41,955
Looks like you guys are having a blast.

79
00:08:44,340 --> 00:08:47,540
What brings a retired
civilian to a place like this?

80
00:08:48,862 --> 00:08:51,182
Came all the way from Okinawa
to do some city sightseeing?

81
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,268
Finally, I get to see you.

82
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:16,517
Hana-chan!

83
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,517
Kin-chan!

84
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:21,228
Long time no see, Kin-chan.

85
00:09:21,311 --> 00:09:23,657
You went straight and ran
off to Okinawa without a word.

86
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:24,897
Sorry about that.

87
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:28,296
You guys were in the middle of a turf war
with Kansai back then. Looked pretty busy.

88
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:31,117
Yeah, it was a real mess,

89
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,057
but you still could've given me a heads-up.

90
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:32,997
Don't be a stranger.

91
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,596
We've known each other since preschool.

92
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:36,777
Right, the Peach Class.

93
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:39,180
The Peach Class... that takes me back!

94
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,776
Looks like you're doing well for yourself.

95
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,340
Couldn't be better.

96
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:47,087
Hey, Hana-chan.

97
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:49,276
I've been hearing some bad
rumors about the main family.

98
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:51,127
Hmm? Like what?

99
00:09:51,210 --> 00:09:54,810
Jacking up the tribute fees out of nowhere,
and trying to take over the Kirii-gumi's turf?

100
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:58,427
- Turf?
- Yeah.

101
00:09:58,510 --> 00:09:59,510
What turf?

102
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:03,137
Besides,

103
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:06,597
the tribute fees haven't
changed since my old man's time.

104
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,200
Huh? They haven't?

105
00:10:10,340 --> 00:10:11,370
Then

106
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:13,330
who's behind this?

107
00:10:28,086 --> 00:10:29,379
Ihashi.

108
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:31,940
Why did you kidnap Kin-chan?

109
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:39,277
Chairman,

110
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,265
there's a reason for this.

111
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:42,400
Was it to keep Kin-chan
and me from meeting?

112
00:10:44,686 --> 00:10:46,020
Please, let me explain.

113
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:53,060
Explain?

114
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:55,400
Yes.

115
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:57,448
An explanation.

116
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:14,080
Whoa, hey.

117
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:16,880
I was born into a yakuza family, you know.

118
00:11:18,469 --> 00:11:21,055
I've been playing with
guns since preschool.

119
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,440
You really think you can beat me?

120
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:27,180
Hey.

121
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:28,800
Run, run!

122
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:30,100
Hurry up!

123
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:41,217
Wait.

124
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,369
Please, wait!

125
00:11:42,452 --> 00:11:43,620
Chairman!

126
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:49,620
Hey, get in here.

127
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:57,360
Quit stalling.

128
00:12:04,060 --> 00:12:05,183
I beg you.

129
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:06,720
Please don't kill me.

130
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:12,437
Seriously,

131
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:15,818
cooking the syndicate's books
and then begging for your life?

132
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:20,000
Have you no shame?

133
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:26,800
You...

134
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:32,500
Weren't you killed and encased in concrete?

135
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:36,040
That was a lie.

136
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:38,250
A lie?

137
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:43,263
This guy spilled everything.

138
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:47,020
Cooking the books to embezzle money,

139
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:51,312
using it to buy up land in Awakuma
City and pay off street thugs...

140
00:12:55,190 --> 00:12:57,870
He said you were the one behind it all.

141
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:06,000
He was a tough nut to crack.

142
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:09,220
Took us forever to get him to talk.

143
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:14,268
Seems like he's really terrified of you.

144
00:13:24,380 --> 00:13:25,780
Now I remember.

145
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:29,000
You used to be with the Kirii-gumi.

146
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:32,787
You were one of my dad's men.

147
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:40,610
(Summer 1998)

148
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:47,368
Boss Kataoka.

149
00:13:48,578 --> 00:13:49,097
I got what you asked for.

150
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:51,177
Oh, Ihashi. Thanks for the trouble.

151
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:52,260
Not at all.

152
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,850
Today's my boy's birthday.

153
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:56,897
Congratulations.

154
00:13:56,980 --> 00:13:58,540
We haven't been able to see each other,

155
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,548
so this is the first time.

156
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:02,216
I'm celebrating it with him.

157
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,397
Here's some premium sushi, take a look.

158
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:06,317
How should I know?

159
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:07,440
Come on, please take it...

160
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:08,514
Don't be like that.

161
00:14:10,970 --> 00:14:12,890
- Good work.
- It's the boss.

162
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:16,310
- Good work today, Boss.
- Oh, Kataoka.

163
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:18,520
Out of the way!

164
00:14:21,770 --> 00:14:23,029
Die!

165
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:47,445
You bastard!

166
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:53,300
Kin... Kinji...

167
00:14:54,890 --> 00:14:56,187
Kataoka!

168
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:57,097
Are you alright?

169
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:58,270
Stay with me!

170
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,500
Kataoka.

171
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,880
Hang in there, Kataoka!

172
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:06,420
Kataoka!

173
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:13,840
I... I...

174
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:16,600
You kidnapped me instead of killing me.

175
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:19,637
Was that to repay the debt you owed my dad?

176
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:22,680
You wanted to spare my life
and send me back to Okinawa.

177
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:42,220
Ihashi,

178
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:45,840
you're done for.

179
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:14,937
Kataoka-san, Odajima-san,
are you guys okay?

180
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:18,720
Come at me, all of you!

181
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:20,770
Huh?

182
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:32,210
Ihashi...

183
00:16:35,570 --> 00:16:36,570
What?

184
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:41,797
Yo.

185
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,497
Managing Director, and the young guy.

186
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:44,880
Kataoka-san.

187
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,500
Oh.

188
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:49,130
From the Kirii-gumi?

189
00:16:51,130 --> 00:16:52,477
The Chairman of the main family!

190
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:53,560
What?

191
00:16:58,260 --> 00:16:59,560
What's going on here?

192
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:02,147
Anyway,

193
00:17:02,230 --> 00:17:03,600
everything's settled now.

194
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:05,580
Thanks for coming.

195
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:07,597
Right...

196
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:08,680
Yes, sir.

197
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:13,574
By the way,

198
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:16,080
is this the one?

199
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:18,740
Yeah.

200
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:33,967
Kin-chan,

201
00:17:34,050 --> 00:17:35,880
your taste in women sure has changed.

202
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:38,347
Come on.

203
00:17:38,430 --> 00:17:41,010
You used to go for the
busty, bombshell types, right?

204
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:46,280
He may not be busty,

205
00:17:50,270 --> 00:17:51,790
but he's got serious guts.

206
00:17:52,530 --> 00:17:53,960
He's the best wife I could ask for.

207
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,300
I'm starving.

208
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,610
Boss.

209
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:17,720
Boss...

210
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:19,680
You came.

211
00:18:21,470 --> 00:18:22,760
More or less.

212
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:25,480
It's our family's mess, after all.

213
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,380
I'm here to see how it plays out.

214
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:33,740
You're still alive, huh?

215
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:37,020
Thanks for your concern.

216
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:52,539
The heads of the Kotoku-kai
and Kirii-gumi are sworn enemies.

217
00:18:52,953 --> 00:18:57,093
You said a war would
break out if they ever met...

218
00:18:58,540 --> 00:18:59,840
This is bad.

219
00:19:56,110 --> 00:19:57,671
Some things never change.

220
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:00,720
See, the two of them...

221
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:02,860
back when they were in kindergarten...

222
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:09,934
- Kei-chan, give me your finger! - Huh?

223
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,837
Pinky swear, make a vow.

224
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:16,797
Tell a lie and you swallow
a thousand needles.

225
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,740
There, our pact is sealed!

226
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:21,777
Wait, wasn't that just a pinky swear?

227
00:20:21,860 --> 00:20:25,997
Our two families are
uniting, so it's a blood pact!

228
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:27,437
Uniting?

229
00:20:27,520 --> 00:20:29,440
They said it's just like getting married.

230
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:34,720
Which means you and I are
getting married, Kei-chan!

231
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:37,737
I don't get it.

232
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:57,760
Ever since then, Hana-chan
has been proposing to Keito.

233
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:01,760
They're still kissing...

234
00:21:09,477 --> 00:21:12,288
Kei-chan, I missed you so much.

235
00:21:14,060 --> 00:21:16,580
You never show up to
the executive meetings.

236
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:18,800
It's always that old guy instead.

237
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:22,907
Still, it's so good to finally see you.

238
00:21:23,980 --> 00:21:25,201
Kei-chan.

239
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:26,744
Do you want a castle?

240
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:27,827
Huh?

241
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:30,420
I'm about to get my hands on one.

242
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:32,300
I'll give it to you as a present.

243
00:21:35,020 --> 00:21:36,320
So...

244
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:39,440
Let's get married.

245
00:21:40,150 --> 00:21:41,150
Kei-chan.

246
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:42,750
Oh.

247
00:21:46,370 --> 00:21:47,840
I'll kill you.

248
00:21:48,850 --> 00:21:50,050
Kei-chan?

249
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:52,457
I'm gonna kill you!

250
00:21:52,540 --> 00:21:53,540
Huh?

251
00:21:54,271 --> 00:21:55,564
This means all-out war!

252
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:59,418
What war, Kei-chan?!

253
00:22:00,152 --> 00:22:01,152
Let go of me!

254
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:06,907
Wait, I'm dead serious! I'll
give you the whole castle!

255
00:22:06,990 --> 00:22:08,552
Who the hell wants a castle?!

256
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:12,020
Then how about a tank?

257
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:15,977
Or do you just want me?

258
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:17,560
You're the last thing I want!

259
00:22:18,940 --> 00:22:20,140
Who else is there besides me?!

260
00:22:20,214 --> 00:22:21,460
Hey, Kei-chan!

261
00:22:22,216 --> 00:22:23,593
Is there someone else?!

262
00:22:23,676 --> 00:22:24,676
Knock it off!

263
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:27,722
Hold him back, hold him back!

264
00:22:27,805 --> 00:22:29,282
I'll follow you to the ends of the earth!

265
00:22:29,306 --> 00:22:30,386
Good, keep him right there.

266
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,000
(Finale Preview)

267
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:44,200
I will protect the Boss.

268
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:47,400
I swear,

269
00:22:48,260 --> 00:22:49,560
I won't let you die.

270
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:51,800
As long as I'm with you,

271
00:22:53,700 --> 00:22:55,560
we're together, in life or in death.

272
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:58,377
This time,

273
00:22:59,550 --> 00:23:01,230
I'll protect you, no matter what.

274
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:03,465
If...

275
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:05,593
forever really exists.
